  {
   "pair": "information_valuation + selective_attention",
   "role": "buffering",
   "sd": 0.058980536651540544,
   "sign3": true,
   "heading": "Buffering example  –  information valuation + selective attention",
   "observations": "Observations. In all 6 dimensions the real combination stays below the additive expectation – by up to −0.60 in Novelty/uncertainty & sensory behavior (additive 0.60 → real 0.00) – and the pair reads at or near the intact baseline everywhere (largest residual Δ 0.08). No dimension emerges that neither single factor had reached. All 3 replicates agree at the 6-dimension aggregate level (SD 0.059); the error bars give the per-dimension replicate SD.",
   "possible_cause": "Possible cause of buffering. Both lesions cut the same upstream gate: valuation decides whether an information gap is worth pursuing at all, and selective attention decides which of the parallel channels is let through. Cut both and the stream is severed before it reaches the dimensions the other lesion would have disturbed – the second lesion removes the route along which the first one’s damage would be expressed. The pair therefore saturates instead of adding, and the additive expectation (a linear extrapolation) over-predicts: it assumes a pathway that is already off.",
